It is vendored (not fetched at runtime) so the aish plugin is self-contained
and reproducible. Local modifications made for the aish integration (SPR-073)
are marked inline in `cclimits.sh` with `TASK-319` / "Local modifications"
comments, chiefly:

  * compute_pace() made portable across GNU coreutils `date` (Linux) and BSD
    `date` (macOS); upstream used BSD-only `date -j` flags.
  * Graceful degradation: pace is omitted rather than aborting when a reset
    timestamp cannot be parsed.

